# Settings for running Bilibi on your own machine with ./bilibi start.
#
# Copy this file to .env, which Git never commits, and remove the # in front
# of a line to change that setting. A variable set in your shell wins over
# this file. Only the lines below are read; anything else is ignored with a
# message. Servers never read this file: install-server.sh writes each server
# instance its own env file (docs/server-install.md).
#
# For an application made with the app maker, .env belongs in the application
# root, next to its ./bilibi command, not inside sources/platform.

# The address of this instance: a name under .localhost, served over HTTPS.
# Default: bilibi.localhost for the Bilibi Platform checkout; an application is
# named after its origin repository, so SB-Tape/sbg-bilibi becomes
# sbg-bilibi.localhost. Each instance on your machine needs a different name.
#BILIBI_DEV_HOST=my-bilibi.localhost

# The port Bilibi itself listens on behind Caddy. Default: the first free port
# from 4300 up. With this set, a checkout never claims bilibi.localhost first;
# name it with BILIBI_DEV_HOST as well.
#BILIBI_DEV_PORT=4300

# Open the sign-in page in your browser when the app is ready: 1 or 0.
#BILIBI_OPEN_BROWSER=1
